{"v":1,"accession":"PRJNA1025325","title":"sludge samples collected from the  pyridine degradation reactors with different co-metabolites","description":"The efficiency of traditional pyridine degradation systems is subpar, and nitrogen removal is given less consideration. This study elucidated the synchronous removal performance of pyridine and pyridine-N when glucose or phenol were added and demonstrated the co-metabolic mechanism. Glucose could speed up pyridine oxidation and improve TN removal effectiveness by enhancing ammonia assimilation. Phenol would hinder pyridine from degrading, although it might remove TN through denitrification.","center":"Zhengzhou University","data_type":"Raw sequence reads","submission_date":"2023/10/07 00:00","sample_cols":["accession","title","tier","context","collection_date","collection_year","country","region","place_id","place","location_status","lat","lon","submitted_location","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","eligibility_reason"],"samples":[["SAMN37720718","activity sludge sample","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2019-03-06",2019,"CN","Henan",1784658,"Zhengzhou","verified",null,null,"China: Zhengzhou","aerobic reactor",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN37720719","activity sludge sample","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2019-05-07",2019,"CN","Henan",1784658,"Zhengzhou","verified",null,null,"China: Zhengzhou","aerobic reactor",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN37720720","activity sludge sample","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2019-05-08",2019,"CN","Henan",1784658,"Zhengzhou","verified",null,null,"China: Zhengzhou","aerobic reactor",null,null,null,"city-level location without sample-site confirmation"],["SAMN37720721","activity sludge sample","probable_urban","municipal_wastewater","2019-05-09",2019,"CN","Henan",1784658,"Zhengzhou","verified",null,null,"China: Zhengzhou","aerobic react